-- Raw L4 where FEEL was wanted, beside a decision that is plain FEEL. `as
-- text` becomes a boxed literal whose text is L4 (Blocking D-LITERALEXPR), and
-- `banded`'s first test becomes an input column whose text is L4 (Blocking
-- D-NONFEELINPUT). Neither engine runs any decision of such a file, `pay`
-- included: KIE 8.44 refuses to load it and Camunda 8.7.6 to parse it, and
-- both notes say so.
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `as text` x IS x AS STRING

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `banded` x IS
  IF x AS STRING EQUALS "1" THEN 1
  ELSE IF x > 5 THEN 2
            ELSE 3

GIVEN h IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pay` h IS h PLUS 1
